# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  emot3 - .gitignore
#
#  Scoped to what this repo actually produces / consumes:
#    - MSBuild build outputs (per Configuration x Platform)
#    - Visual Studio per-user / per-machine state
#    - Generated resource files (rewritten on every build by gen_rc.py)
#    - Python bytecode cache from running the codegen
#    - Editor / agent local state (.vs, .idea, .vscode, .claude)
#
#  Trimmed from the stock GitHub VisualStudio template - the long list of
#  Azure / NuGet / NCrunch / LightSwitch / etc. patterns doesn't apply to
#  a single C++ DLL project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---- Build outputs --------------------------------------------------------
# MSBuild writes every per-configuration output under build\<Config>\x64\ (DLL +
# obj\ intermediates), so build/ is the single output root - each config gets
# its own folder and incremental database. The .exp / .lib are import-library
# by-products of the DLL we don't ship; the DLL itself is published via the
# GitHub Actions release workflow, not from a local build.
build/

*.dll
*.exp
*.lib
*.obj
*.pdb
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.ilk
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.recipe
*.log


# ---- Generated source -----------------------------------------------------
# tools/gen_rc.py overwrites these every build from the PNGs in resources/.
# Source of truth is the PNG set; tracking the outputs only churns diffs.
src/generated/emot3.rc
src/generated/ResourcesGenerated.cpp


# ---- Visual Studio cache / per-user state ---------------------------------
# .vs/ holds IntelliSense DB, browse data, etc. *.user is per-developer
# debugger config (launch args, working dir). All safe to regenerate.
.vs/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Intellisense / browse databases
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb
*.ipch
ipch/


# ---- Other editors / tools ------------------------------------------------
# .idea/.vscode are JetBrains / VS Code project dirs. .claude holds Claude Code
# workspace state (settings, local overrides) - all per-developer, not shared.
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/


# ---- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/gen_rc.py is plain Python with no third-party deps, but Windows
# Python still drops a __pycache__ next to it on each run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc


# ---- OS noise -------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
